An :IF condition the author split after a trailing `.AND.` (the legacy
shape the style guide's continuation_line_breaks calls Bad): no `;` is
forced after the operator and the continuation takes one level past the
:IF line. The wrapper never moves a source break, so the operator stays
trailing (fmt.max_line_length: "an operator the author left trailing at a
line end stays trailing"). The leading-operator form is left out: range
formatting an operator-led line re-indents it and appends `;` to the line
before it, an A2 invariant failure reported separately.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE CheckLimits;
:PARAMETERS nLow, nHigh, sMode;
:DECLARE bOk;
bOk := .F.;
:IF nLow > 1 .AND.
nHigh < 50 .AND.
          sMode == "STRICT";
bOk := .T.;
:ENDIF;
:RETURN bOk;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE CheckLimits;
	:PARAMETERS nLow, nHigh, sMode;
	:DECLARE bOk;
	bOk := .F.;
	:IF nLow > 1 .AND.
		nHigh < 50 .AND.
		sMode == "STRICT";
		bOk := .T.;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN bOk;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
